Z||000012||DXR_DAD||03-07-2001||02:01 AM||||Standard- A 50 gallon long tank isn't exactly small either.  10 to 15 gallon for a baby or juvenile is cool.  Try to avoid glass and get plexy-glass if you can.  It's really all up to snake as fare as eating goes.  My Boa will not eat frozen mice, so I feed it live mice.  When you buy mice or rats use common sense in sizing.  $250 is way more then enough for a Columbian Red Tail, pay no more then $100.  The other South American Red Tails are more expensive like a Peruvian.  Good luck man.||||reg||1
